import type { Finding } from "../finding.page-type.types.ts"

export const aGeneratedFileHoldsEveryPathItImportsFromAgainstAnyMove = {
  id: "01a08878-e69d-743e-b907-59decbc5078b",
  pageTypeSlug: "finding",
  type: "finding",
  slug: "a-generated-file-holds-every-path-it-imports-from-against-any-move",
  domain: "domain/change",
  claim:
    "A move rewrites the relative specifiers of every body importing what moved, and `generated-file-not-written` refuses the change where any of those bodies is generated. So a generated file importing from outside its own folder holds every path it imports from: nothing under those paths can move, and the property whose relocation would remove the import cannot move either, because relocating it rewrites the same generated file. `alan/track/days` is held by this today, by one import on one line.",
  evidence:
    'The deadlock, both halves refused. `akasha change draft move-folder` with `at: alan/track/days` and `to: alan/track/daily/days` answered ``\\`alan/chess/games/chess-game.page-type.types.ts\\` is generated, and a generated file is written by the thing that generates it rather than by hand``. `akasha change draft move-page` with `at: alan/track/days/properties/played-at.instant-property.ts` and `to: alan/chess/games/properties` answered the same words. The second is the mend for the first, and the same guard refuses it for the same reason.\n\nThe one line holding it. `alan/chess/games/chess-game.page-type.types.ts:4` reads `import type { PlayedAt } from "../../track/days/properties/played-at.instant-property.ts"`. Searching every generated kind — `.types.ts`, `.worked.ts`, `.addressed.ts`, `.entries.ts` — for `track/days` matches that file and no other. One import in one generated body holds 784 tracked files and 33 sidecars where they are.\n\nWhy the property is misfiled to begin with. `alan/chess/games/chess-game.page-type.ts:18` names `instant-property/played-at` in its `parts` and :43 names it again in `properties`. `alan/track/days/day.page-type.ts` names it in neither. `parts.relation-property.ts` gives `A page is named by exactly one parent`, so the parent of `played-at` is `chess-game`, and the other fifteen properties `chess-game` declares all sit at `alan/chess/games/properties/`. `played-at` is used by `alan/track/days/properties/listens.page-property-entry.ts:21` as a property of the `listens` entry shape, but using a property is not declaring it.\n\nWhere the guard draws its line. `changes/guards/pages/generated-file-not-written/generated-file-not-written.change-guard.code.ts` reads `given.said.edits`, skips anything that is not a `replace`, and allows a replace only where `landed.get(one.path)` is defined and that source path is itself generated — that is, where the generated file travels as the destination of a move. A generated file rewritten in place, having not moved, has no entry in `landed`, so it is refused. That allowance is what lets a `.page-type.types.ts` travel inside a folder that moves, and it is why the calendar moves landed while this one does not.\n\nThe mend, and why it costs nothing. The move does not need to rewrite generated files at all, because the generator rewrites them anyway. `commands/modules/type-generating/type-generating.module.code.ts` gives `couldTurn(change)` answering true where any changed path is a bare `page-type` page, a `.type-generator.ts` or a `.types.ts`; the days move carries `alan/track/days/day.page-type.ts`, which is a bare page-type page, so `couldTurn` answers true. `typedOver` then reads `shadow.index.everyOfType(PAGE_TYPE)` — every page type in the tree, rather than only the ones that moved — and writes each generated body again from the shadow, emitting a `replace` only where the new text differs. `chess-game` is in that reading, and the body it would write carries the moved path. `typesFor` is called from `change-preparing` at :110, after the change has answered and after guards have run, so those generator edits are not judged by this guard. If a move left generated bodies alone and let the generator answer for them, both refusals above would go and the written result would be the same.\n\nHow wide this reaches. Counting `from "../` in every `*.page-type.types.ts` and `*.module.types.ts`: `alan/chess/progresses/chess-progress.page-type.types.ts` has 5, `chess-game.page-type.types.ts` has 4, and `change-guarding.module.types.ts`, three `all-about-alan` page types, `category-rule`, `mobile-cut`, `book-record` and `agents/agent.page-type.types.ts` have 3 each. Every one of those paths is held the same way.\n\nNot established. I did not read `generatedIn`, so this describes which edits the guard refuses rather than how it decides a path is generated. I did not seek an ordering of changes escaping the deadlock beyond the two drafts above, and I did not test whether an unchecked change kind passes the guard. I did not measure how many folders across the tree are held by this, only that the eleven files above hold at least 32 paths between them.',
} as const satisfies Finding
